From dd4e4810b5b2391d7ba611032cbdfe767d4e358c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:17:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Android: keep the phone's world running while the player
 is in another app

Android freezes an app's processes a few seconds after it leaves the
screen, and the world's server, a child of the app, froze with it unless
the world was shared: only sharing started the foreground service. A DM
turn the AI was answering stopped where it was, so a player who checked
another app came back to a table still waiting on the DM, the answer
never arriving. The perf plan already noted it for Wi-Fi hosting
(docs/perf-and-bugs-plan-1.0.md A, "LAN-only hosting freezes when the app
is backgrounded").

The service now runs whenever the world does: quietly ("Your world is
running") while the player plays alone, and as before ("Your world is
shared", with Stop hosting) while a tunnel is up. Ending a share, by the
button, by a failure or by cloudflared closing, leaves the quiet
notification for a world still running; the world stopping (the
bridge's idle stop, Stop, the server dying) or the app being swiped away
removes it. Android 12+ refuses a foreground service started from the
background, so the service starts when the world comes up, its
notification is replaced in place afterwards, and a refused start leaves
the world running as before.

